  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>National Payments Corporation of India: product statistics (UPI, BHIM, IMPS, NETC FASTag, AePS, NACH and its mandate system, CTS, e-RUPI), UPI ecosystem statistics (P2P and P2M, apps, merchant categories and segments, states and districts) and daily statistics, as published on npci.org.in and captured by our archive from the data service behind those pages. Last captured <b id="prov-captured" set:html={N["prov-captured"]}></b>. Data vintage: <span id="prov-vintage" set:html={N["prov-vintage"]}></span> (NPCI edits past rows in place and dates none of them).</p>
        <p>Checked by hand against NPCI's tables: UPI in September 2026, 24,068.38 million transactions worth ₹29,37,396.67 crore, identical in NPCI's product table and its P2P and P2M table; Maharashtra in September 2026, 2,364.51 million transactions, 9.82% of UPI.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Method</h6>
        <p>Counts and rupees as NPCI prints them, scaled from million and crore. Averages, shares and rates are computed here and labelled where shown. Each rebuild checks that NPCI's parts add to its totals, that its daily rows add to its months, that its two UPI tables agree and that its UPI agrees with the RBI's; every place NPCI's own figures disagree is named in the data notes and kept as printed. Printed state and district shares that contradict NPCI's own counts are left out.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions and breaks</h6>
        <p>NPCI edits past rows without notice. BHIM's count changed in April 2020 and the cheque grids merged in November 2023; both are drawn apart, never joined. NPCI's website now refuses automated reading, so new months reach this guide only when our archive captures them; a capture is never filled in by hand.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Version 1.0, built October 2026 from data to {MU}. NPCI's other tables (RuPay, the monthly ATM network table, Bharat BillPay and UPI's archived tables) are not yet in our archive.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
